"Panel window": `window_classname("NSPanel")` makes a macOS window winit's non-activating panel.

Applies to: tauri-runtime-cef 3.0.0-alpha.7 (crates.io) + 0001, 0003, 0004, 0005, 0006,
applied in vendor/tauri-runtime-cef. Not offered upstream.

Why: Eos's quick panel (07 §4.3) must take the keyboard over another app without activating
Eos or taking the menu bar. winit builds such a window (`WindowAttributesMacOS::with_panel`:
an `NSPanel` subclass with `NSWindowStyleMaskNonactivatingPanel` that can become key), but
Tauri's window builder offers no macOS attribute that reaches it. `window_classname` is the
one builder call that is a no-op on macOS (it names a Windows window class), so the name
`NSPanel` (`PANEL_CLASS`) asks for the panel there. Changing an existing window's class
afterwards does not work: winit's delegate observes the window's `effectiveAppearance`, and
AppKit's forwarded key-value observation breaks when the class changes under it (an
`NSRangeException` when the window is released).

